    <node id="Source Image">
      <data key="d0">Source Image</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An image received from the camera that includes a plurality of representations of a plurality of faces to be compared against member images.&lt;SEP&gt;An image received from the camera that includes a plurality of representations of a plurality of faces.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Search Term">
      <data key="d0">Search Term</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A term received from the user interface of the application, compared to member descriptors by the search service.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Face Recognition">
      <data key="d0">Face Recognition</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The technique of comparing representations of faces in a source image to representations of faces in member images to identify matching members.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User Interface">
      <data key="d0">User Interface</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An interface provided by the application through which a user supplies at least one friend identifier and optionally a friend level indicator.&lt;SEP&gt;An interface provided by the application that receives at least one search term or friend identifier from the user.&lt;SEP&gt;An interface rendered on a client for displaying video content features and receiving user interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;An interface through which explicit user feedback favoring the first fictional character is obtained.&lt;SEP&gt;An interface that displays the generated relationship data.&lt;SEP&gt;A user interface on which the model of relationships or relationship data is displayed, optionally providing a graphical representation of relationship strength.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8917913B2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;US10778629B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US10778629B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US10778629B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Result">
      <data key="d0">Result</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Output from the search service identifying at least one member who is a friend of the identified member and whose member image face matches a face in the source image. It may include a first result and a second result.&lt;SEP&gt;A result identifying a member who has a member descriptor matching the search term and a member image with a face matching a face in the source image, sent back to the mobile device.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Indicium">
      <data key="d0">Indicium</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A marker used to augment the source image on the screen to identify a matched member. It may include a first indicium and a second indicium.&lt;SEP&gt;A marker used to augment the source image on the screen of the mobile device to identify a matching member.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Friend Identifier">
      <data key="d0">Friend Identifier</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An identifier received from the user interface that identifies a member whose friends are to be searched. It may comprise a plurality of friend identifiers.&lt;SEP&gt;An identifier received from the user interface of the application in an alternative embodiment of the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Camera">
      <data key="d0">Camera</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A component of the mobile device that captures source images containing representations of faces, in operative communication with the application.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of the mobile device in operative communication with the application, providing at least one source image.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Screen">
      <data key="d0">Screen</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A display component of the mobile device on which results are shown by augmenting the source image with indicia identifying matched members.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of the mobile device on which results are displayed by augmenting the source image with indicia.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Face Representation">
      <data key="d0">Face Representation</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A representation of a face contained in a source image or member image, used for comparison by the search service.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Friend Level Indicator">
      <data key="d0">Friend Level Indicator</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An indicator received from the user interface that the search service uses to perform iterative searching of friends-of-friends.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Match">
      <data key="d0">Match</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The determination that a face representation in a member image corresponds to a face representation in the source image, which may be an essentially exact match or an approximate match within a degree of confidence.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Friends-Of-Friends Search">
      <data key="d0">Friends-Of-Friends Search</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An iterative searching technique performed by the search service based at least in part upon the friend level indicator and the friend identifier.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mobile Phone">
      <data key="d0">Mobile Phone</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of mobile device that may be used in the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tablet">
      <data key="d0">Tablet</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of mobile device that may be used in the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PDA">
      <data key="d0">PDA</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A personal digital assistant, a type of mobile device that may be used in the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dedicated Camera">
      <data key="d0">Dedicated Camera</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of mobile device that may be used in the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">US8917913B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US8917913B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284306</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="US9514120B1">
      <data key="d0">US9514120B1</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A patent document titled "Classification of a string as a typographical error based on feedback" describing a method for identifying and classifying potential typographical errors in a work using user feedback.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Computing Device">
      <data key="d0">Computing Device</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A device hosting a server that identifies potential typographical errors in a work, sends data to users, collects and combines feedback, sorts the feedback, and updates an initial reference.&lt;SEP&gt;A device that executes computer instructions and applications to perform content recommendation functions.&lt;SEP&gt;A device that executes an application to render content, obtain interaction data, identify characters, calculate relationship scores, and generate recommendations.&lt;SEP&gt;A device comprising at least one computing device that executes the plurality of computer instructions stored on the non-transitory computer-readable medium.&lt;SEP&gt;One or more devices that execute machine-readable instructions to perform the described operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;US9218390B2-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US9218390B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284503</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Processing Device">
      <data key="d0">Processing Device</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A device that executes the method steps including identifying potential typographical errors, sending data, receiving feedback, combining and sorting feedback, determining acceptable strings, and updating references.&lt;SEP&gt;A device that performs operations such as determining author-intended strings, combining feedback, sorting feedback, and updating parameter-specific references.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Initial Reference">
      <data key="d0">Initial Reference</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference used to identify potential typographical errors in a work, which is updated to include acceptable strings.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Work">
      <data key="d0">Work</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A document or text comprising a plurality of words in which potential typographical errors are identified.&lt;SEP&gt;A creative or informational piece comprising a plurality of words that may contain potential typographical errors and author-intended strings.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Potential Typographical Error">
      <data key="d0">Potential Typographical Error</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A string in a work identified as a possible typographical error using an initial reference, which may be an author-intended string or an actual error.&lt;SEP&gt;A string in a work that may be a typographical error but could also be an author-intended string, subject to feedback and determination by users and processing devices.&lt;SEP&gt;A string identified as a possible typographical error, whose presence is indicated by data comprising the string, its position in the work, or its context.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Author-Intended String">
      <data key="d0">Author-Intended String</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A string that is intentionally used by an author, comprising author-intended spelling, punctuation, grammar, or use of foreign language words.&lt;SEP&gt;A string in a work that is intentionally written by the author, comprising an author-intended spelling, punctuation, grammar, or use of foreign language words, and identified as such rather than being an actual typographical error.&lt;SEP&gt;A string that is intended by the author, used as a basis for sorting combined feedback and updating a reference.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Acceptable String">
      <data key="d0">Acceptable String</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A potential typographical error determined to be an author-intended string based on sorted user feedback, added to the initial reference.&lt;SEP&gt;A string identified as acceptable (author-intended) when its associated percentage of feedback exceeds a threshold percentage.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Actual Error">
      <data key="d0">Actual Error</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A potential typographical error determined not to be author-intended, associated with an alternative string.&lt;SEP&gt;A potential typographical error identified as an actual error when its associated percentage of feedback does not exceed the threshold percentage, with an alternative string associated with it.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alternative String">
      <data key="d0">Alternative String</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A string associated with an actual error as a correction or replacement.&lt;SEP&gt;A string associated with an actual error as a replacement or correction.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User Feedback">
      <data key="d0">User Feedback</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Feedback collected from users for a work indicating whether potential typographical errors are author-intended strings, comprising user identifier, work identifier, string, position, decision, confidence level, and parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Explicit user feedback expressing that the user favors the first fictional character, obtained via a user interface as described in claim 23.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284456</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Combined Feedback">
      <data key="d0">Combined Feedback</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Feedback for a work combined with feedback for additional works.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback from a plurality of users for a work combined with feedback for additional works, generated by a processing device.&lt;SEP&gt;A combined feedback generated from one or more additional works, which is sorted based on one or more parameters associated with an author-intended string.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sorted Feedback">
      <data key="d0">Sorted Feedback</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Combined feedback sorted based on one or more selected parameters associated with the work.&lt;SEP&gt;Combined feedback sorted based on selected parameters associated with a work, such as author, title, topic, or publisher.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback resulting from sorting the combined feedback based on parameters associated with the author-intended string.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Selected Parameters">
      <data key="d0">Selected Parameters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parameters used to sort combined feedback, comprising an author, a title, a topic, or a publisher associated with the work.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Author">
      <data key="d0">Author</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A person associated with a work, used as a parameter for sorting feedback and for parameter-specific references.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter associated with a work, used in sorting combined feedback and in parameter-specific references.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Title">
      <data key="d0">Title</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The title associated with a work, used as a parameter for sorting feedback and for parameter-specific references.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topic">
      <data key="d0">Topic</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The topic associated with a work, used as a parameter for sorting feedback and for parameter-specific references.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Publisher">
      <data key="d0">Publisher</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The publisher associated with a work, used as a parameter for sorting feedback and for parameter-specific references.&lt;SEP&gt;A parameter associated with a work, used in sorting combined feedback and in parameter-specific references.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parameter-Specific Reference">
      <data key="d0">Parameter-Specific Reference</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference generated based on an acceptable string, corresponding to a parameter, comprising an author-specific reference, title-specific reference, topic-specific reference, or publisher-specific reference.&lt;SEP&gt;A reference specific to a parameter (author, title, topic, or publisher) that is updated using author-intended strings, including author-specific, title-specific, topic-specific, and publisher-specific references.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parameter-Specific Statistics">
      <data key="d0">Parameter-Specific Statistics</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Statistics compiled based on sorted feedback, used to determine whether a potential typographical error is an acceptable string when exceeding a threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistics compiled based on sorted feedback, including counts and percentages of users marking potential typographical errors as author-intended strings for a parameter.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Threshold Percentage">
      <data key="d0">Threshold Percentage</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A percentage threshold that sorted feedback identifying a potential typographical error as an author-intended string must exceed to classify it as an acceptable string.&lt;SEP&gt;A percentage threshold used to determine whether a potential typographical error is an acceptable string (author-intended) or an actual error.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Transitory Computer-Readable Medium">
      <data key="d0">Non-Transitory Computer-Readable Medium</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A medium having instructions stored thereon that, when executed by a processing device, cause the processing device to perform operations for classifying typographical errors.&lt;SEP&gt;A medium storing instructions that, when executed, cause operations for determining author-intended strings, combining and sorting feedback, and updating parameter-specific references.&lt;SEP&gt;A medium having computer instructions executable by a computing device to perform content recommendation functions.&lt;SEP&gt;A medium having computer instructions executable by a computing device to perform content rendering, character preference determination, and recommendation generation.&lt;SEP&gt;A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing computer instructions, referenced in claims 22-25, that causes a computing device to perform operations related to media content and fictional character relationship scoring.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US9374411B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284456</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Users">
      <data key="d0">Users</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A plurality of users who receive data indicative of potential typographical errors and provide feedback for a work.&lt;SEP&gt;Users to whom item recommendations are presented.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Feedback">
      <data key="d0">Feedback</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Information provided by users regarding a work, including user identifiers, work identifiers, strings identified as potential typographical errors, positions of strings, decisions on whether strings are author-intended, confidence levels, and associated parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Server Computing Machine">
      <data key="d0">Server Computing Machine</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A server that receives feedback from an apparatus, combines it with additional feedback, sorts the combined feedback, and updates a reference using author-intended strings.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Graphical User Interface">
      <data key="d0">Graphical User Interface</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An interface through which data indicative of a potential typographical error in a work is provided to a user.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Apparatus">
      <data key="d0">Apparatus</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A device comprising a memory and a processing device that provides data on potential typographical errors to users, receives input identifying author-intended strings, determines associated parameters, and provides feedback to a server computing machine.&lt;SEP&gt;A device or system referenced in claims 18, 19, and 20 that processes input, data indicative of potential typographical errors, and generates combined feedback.&lt;SEP&gt;An apparatus comprising means for receiving a data-stream, means for extracting management data, and means for storing management data in a searchable format in a database.&lt;SEP&gt;An apparatus comprising means for receiving a data-stream, carrying out a server function, extracting management data, and storing the management data in a searchable format in a database.&lt;SEP&gt;A device comprising means for receiving data-streams, carrying out a storage router function, and extracting management data.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US9514120B1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;US7756837B2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;US7756837B2-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;US7756837B2-chunk-003</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US7756837B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284549</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Reference">
      <data key="d0">Reference</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference that is updated based on the sorted feedback using the author-intended string.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User Identifier">
      <data key="d0">User Identifier</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An identifier of a user that may be part of the input.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Work Identifier">
      <data key="d0">Work Identifier</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An identifier of a work that may be part of the input.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Position Of String In Work">
      <data key="d0">Position Of String In Work</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The location of a string within a work, which may be part of the input or of the data indicative of a potential typographical error.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Decision">
      <data key="d0">Decision</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A decision indicating whether a corresponding string is an author-intended string, which may be part of the input.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Confidence Level">
      <data key="d0">Confidence Level</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A confidence level of the decision, which may be part of the input.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Context For String In Work">
      <data key="d0">Context For String In Work</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The context surrounding a string in the work, which may be part of the data indicative of a potential typographical error.</data>
      <data key="d3">US9514120B1-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">US9514120B1.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284350</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Personalization Network Service">
      <data key="d0">Personalization Network Service</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A network service that enables developers to develop recommenders made available to content site operators for providing recommendations to end users, and that optimizes the use and selection of recommenders for different end users, groups, segments, content sites, and the like.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Content Site">
      <data key="d0">Content Site</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A site that requests event data storage and item recommendations from the personalization network service over a computer network.&lt;SEP&gt;A site that requests item recommendations from the recommendations system over a computer network via a network service interface, and that may provide recommender selections and weighting selections.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Recommender">
      <data key="d0">Recommender</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A software component that generates item recommendations; recommenders may be external and operated by entities different from the personalization network service provider.&lt;SEP&gt;A component or service provided by a recommender provider that uses collected event data regarding user-generated events to select particular items to recommend to users, and provides scores that are normalized and weighted by the recommendations system.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="External Recommender">
      <data key="d0">External Recommender</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A recommender registered with the recommendations service and provided by entities that differ from the provider of the recommendations service, accessed over the computer network.&lt;SEP&gt;A recommender associated with a plurality of external recommenders, whose provider may provide machine readable descriptions and to which content sites may assign weights.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Recommender Provider">
      <data key="d0">Recommender Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An entity that operates and provides recommenders, separate from the operator of the personalization network service.&lt;SEP&gt;An entity, different from the provider of the recommendations system, that provides recommenders and submits registration submissions to request registration of the recommenders with the recommendations system.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Developer">
      <data key="d0">Developer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A person who develops recommenders that can be made available to content site operators through the personalization network service.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="End User">
      <data key="d0">End User</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A user to whom recommendations are provided by content sites.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Event Data">
      <data key="d0">Event Data</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Data descriptive of user-generated events, comprising identifiers of particular items and particular users to which the events correspond.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Event Data Repository">
      <data key="d0">Event Data Repository</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A repository comprising physical computer storage that stores event data received from content sites.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Network Service Interface">
      <data key="d0">Network Service Interface</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An interface operative to receive requests from a content site over a computer network, including requests to store event data and requests for item recommendations.&lt;SEP&gt;An interface over a computer network through which requests from content sites for item recommendations are received.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Registration Module">
      <data key="d0">Registration Module</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A module configured to provide functionality for registering an external recommender with a recommendations service.&lt;SEP&gt;A module configured to allow a provider of an external recommender to provide machine readable descriptions of the external recommender.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Data Interface">
      <data key="d0">Data Interface</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An interface operative to provide access to event data to a plurality of external recommenders registered with the recommendations service.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Recommendations Service">
      <data key="d0">Recommendations Service</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A service comprising a recommendations retriever that queries external recommenders for recommendations and selects a subset of recommendations to provide to content sites.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Recommendations Retriever">
      <data key="d0">Recommendations Retriever</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A component operative to query external recommenders over the computer network for recommendations and receive recommendations and associated scores.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Optimization Module">
      <data key="d0">Optimization Module</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A module configured to normalize associated scores, assign weights to external recommenders, and optimize recommendations based on user-generated events and previous requests.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Score">
      <data key="d0">Score</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A value associated with a recommendation received from a recommender, which may be normalized and combined with weights to produce overall scores.&lt;SEP&gt;A value assigned to each message by the second pass of the multi-pass message filter, used to indicate whether the message is sorted into an incorrect message folder.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US8069128B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt&lt;SEP&gt;US8069128B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284411</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Overall Score">
      <data key="d0">Overall Score</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A score produced by combining recommender scores with weights, used to select a subset of recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User-Generated Event">
      <data key="d0">User-Generated Event</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An event generated by a user, such as purchase events, item viewing events, and item rating events, used to optimize and adjust recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Computer System">
      <data key="d0">Computer System</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A system comprising computer hardware programmed to implement the network service interface, event data repository, registration module, data interface, recommendations service, and optimization module.&lt;SEP&gt;A system comprising computer hardware that performs the computer-implemented method, and which may comprise multiple physical computing devices.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User Segment">
      <data key="d0">User Segment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A group or segment of end users for which the use and selection of recommenders may be optimized and to which segment-specific weights may be applied.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Registration Submission">
      <data key="d0">Registration Submission</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A submission received from recommender providers that is operative to request registration of recommenders.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Recommendations System">
      <data key="d0">Recommendations System</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A computer-implemented system that registers recommenders from recommender providers, stores access information for the recommenders, receives requests from content sites for item recommendations, causes the recommenders to provide recommendations, normalizes scores, applies weights, and combines scores to generate overall scores for selecting recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User-Generated Events">
      <data key="d0">User-Generated Events</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Events generated by users, comprising one or more of purchase events, item viewing events, and item rating events, used by recommenders to select items to recommend.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Purchase Events">
      <data key="d0">Purchase Events</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of user-generated event involving a user's purchase, used by recommenders in selecting items to recommend.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Item Viewing Events">
      <data key="d0">Item Viewing Events</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of user-generated event involving a user viewing an item, used by recommenders in selecting items to recommend.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Item Rating Events">
      <data key="d0">Item Rating Events</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of user-generated event involving a user rating an item, used by recommenders in selecting items to recommend.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Normalized Scores">
      <data key="d0">Normalized Scores</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Scores produced by normalizing the scores provided by the recommenders, which are combined with weights to generate overall scores.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Weights">
      <data key="d0">Weights</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Values applied to each of the recommenders, which may be based on recommender performance and may be selected by content sites, and are combined with normalized scores to generate overall scores.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Overall Scores">
      <data key="d0">Overall Scores</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Scores generated by combining normalized scores with weights, used in selecting recommendations to provide to content sites.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Uniform Resource Indicators">
      <data key="d0">Uniform Resource Indicators</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Information for accessing the recommenders with the recommendations system, comprising uniform resource indicators.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Computer Data Repository">
      <data key="d0">Computer Data Repository</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A repository that stores information regarding a plurality of recommenders, including network addresses for accessing the recommenders on a network.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Server System">
      <data key="d0">Server System</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A system comprising computer hardware operative to provide a service through which content sites obtain recommendations from a plurality of recommenders for presentation to users, responsive to requests by using network addresses to request recommendations and combining resulting recommendation sets.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Network Addresses">
      <data key="d0">Network Addresses</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Addresses for accessing the recommenders on a network, stored in the computer data repository and used by the server system to request recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Context-Specific Performance">
      <data key="d0">Context-Specific Performance</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance of each recommender in each of a plurality of contexts, monitored by the server system and used to determine how much weight to give to particular recommenders, comprising one or more of user-specific performance, segment-specific performance, and site-specific performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="User-Specific Performance">
      <data key="d0">User-Specific Performance</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of context-specific performance of a recommender relating to specific users.</data>
      <data key="d3">US7991757B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US7991757B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284383</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Segment-Specific Performance">
      <data key="d0">Segment-Specific Performance</data>
