      <data key="d3">US11423041B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US11423041B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284675</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transformed Data Object">
      <data key="d0">Transformed Data Object</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A data object generated by applying an ETL process to one or more source data objects.</data>
      <data key="d3">US11423041B2-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">US11423041B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284675</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="History Object">
      <data key="d0">History Object</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An object created in a history data structure to specify information expected to be stored to describe the performance of an ETL process on a given source data object to generate a transformed data object.&lt;SEP&gt;An object created in a history data structure to specify information expected to be stored to describe the performance of the first ETL process on a given source data object to generate a transformed data object.</data>
      <data key="d3">US11423041B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US11423041B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US11423041B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284675</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="History Data Structure">
      <data key="d0">History Data Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A data structure in which instances of history objects are stored to maintain data lineage for data objects.&lt;SEP&gt;A data structure in which instances of history objects are stored to record information describing the performance of ETL processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">US11423041B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US11423041B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US11423041B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284675</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">One or more conditions against which stored information describing the performance of an ETL process is evaluated to determine whether an event is triggered.&lt;SEP&gt;One of a plurality of different alternative criteria registered for triggering the event, evaluated against stored performance information to determine whether the event should be triggered.</data>
      <data key="d3">US11423041B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US11423041B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US11423041B2.txt</data>
      <data key="d5">1793284675</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Subscriber">
      <data key="d0">Subscriber</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An entity, such as an ETL process or another party, that subscribes to an event and receives notification or is caused to be performed when the event is triggered.&lt;SEP&gt;An entity, such as the second ETL process or another subscriber, that subscribes to an event and receives notification of the event.</data>
      <data key="d3">US11423041B2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;US11423041B2-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">US11423041B2.txt</data>
